## Monetization Strategy

### 2027 (Launch)
- Commissioner fee: $99/league/season
- Projected: 20-80 leagues → $2k-8k

### 2028 (Growth)
- Commissioner fee: $99/season + entry fee rake (10%)
- Projected: 200 leagues + rake → $25k gross, ~$10k net

### 2029 (Scale/Sell Decision)
- SaaS: $19/month per commissioner OR $149/season
- 500 commissioners → $114k ARR
- Acquisition range at this point: $500k-2M (5-20x ARR)

### Growth channels (no paid ads until Year 2)
1. Reddit r/fantasyfootball (2M members)
2. ProductHunt launch
3. Fantasy content creators (free accounts for 10 YouTubers/podcasters)
4. SEO — "season long DFS" "salary cap fantasy football" underserved
5. Referral codes for commissioners

### Acquisition targets (if it takes off)
- DraftKings / FanDuel — acquiring fantasy tools actively
- Sleeper — building "everything fantasy" ecosystem
- Private equity — sports tech very active

